1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,008
[This drama is a work of fiction]

2
00:00:07,008 --> 00:00:08,064
[All scenes involving animals and children
were filmed in compliance with regulations]

3
00:00:08,992 --> 00:00:10,772
Min Seo, why...

4
00:00:10,772 --> 00:00:12,628
Min Seo, who did you hit?

5
00:00:12,628 --> 00:00:14,396
What exactly are you talking about?

6
00:00:14,396 --> 00:00:17,100
So where... where are you supposed to go?

7
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:18,216
I don't know.

8
00:00:18,216 --> 00:00:20,852
We have to hurry. We have to hurry...

9
00:00:33,564 --> 00:00:35,404
Ye Ji.

10
00:00:35,404 --> 00:00:38,652
It's okay, don't worry.

11
00:00:38,652 --> 00:00:40,820
It's okay, it's okay.

12
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:42,916
It's okay, yeah.

13
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:52,924
[Several Months Before the Accident]

14
00:00:55,216 --> 00:00:56,572
Min Seo!

15
00:00:56,572 --> 00:01:00,284
- Honey, watch your head.
- Are you sure you don't want a ride?

16
00:01:00,284 --> 00:01:02,216
- Hello!
- Hello!

17
00:01:02,216 --> 00:01:03,616
We moved into the house across the street.

18
00:01:03,616 --> 00:01:05,484
- Oh, yes, hello.
- Oh, you go to

19
00:01:05,484 --> 00:01:07,500
- Cheongnam Girls' Middle School too?
- Oh, hi.

20
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:08,796
Perfect timing.

21
00:01:08,796 --> 00:01:11,884
We were just about to head to school.
Would you like a ride?

22
00:01:11,884 --> 00:01:15,356
We should save gas and save time
in a country that doesn't produce oil.

23
00:01:15,356 --> 00:01:17,452
And it's good for the girls
to become friends.

24
00:01:17,452 --> 00:01:19,564
Neighbors should help each other out.

25
00:01:19,564 --> 00:01:22,683
Thanks, but maybe not today.

26
00:01:22,683 --> 00:01:27,164
Oh, how about having a meal together
on the weekend?

27
00:01:27,164 --> 00:01:29,804
Just check with your husband and let us know.

28
00:01:29,804 --> 00:01:32,692
I'm actually a pretty good cook.

29
00:01:32,692 --> 00:01:34,349
Oh, okay.

30
00:01:34,349 --> 00:01:39,216
I never imagined someone
this famous would move in next door.

31
00:01:39,216 --> 00:01:42,948
I know. We never imagined we'd end up
living in this neighborhood either.

32
00:01:42,948 --> 00:01:45,764
It's all thanks to our Captain Park.

33
00:01:45,764 --> 00:01:48,020
I see you film all over
different neighborhoods.

34
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:50,364
You're not going to do that here too,
are you?

35
00:01:50,364 --> 00:01:54,483
I'm just not used to
all the noise and commotion.

36
00:01:54,483 --> 00:01:57,649
I stopped by yesterday to drop this off,
but no one was home.

37
00:01:57,649 --> 00:01:58,924
It's a housewarming rice cake.

38
00:01:58,924 --> 00:02:01,692
You don't have to go to
all this trouble next time.

39
00:02:02,796 --> 00:02:05,252
Not at all.

40
00:02:05,252 --> 00:02:08,716
Sometimes too much thoughtfulness
can be a bit overwhelming.

41
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:13,308
Min Seo, get in that car.

42
00:02:13,308 --> 00:02:15,783
Thank you for the ride.

43
00:02:20,388 --> 00:02:22,983
Wow. That's insane.

44
00:02:32,183 --> 00:02:33,983
[GALAXY EXPRESS, Bye Bye Planet]

45
00:02:40,812 --> 00:02:43,083
I like that song too.

46
00:02:45,183 --> 00:02:47,276
[Bye Bye Planet]

47
00:02:47,276 --> 00:02:49,183
Alright, let's go to school.

48
00:02:49,183 --> 00:02:51,628
[Bye Bye Planet]

49
00:02:55,069 --> 00:02:58,016
What's this? What song is this?

50
00:02:59,428 --> 00:03:01,044
Ye Ji, you listen to music like this?

51
00:03:01,044 --> 00:03:04,116
What are you talking about?
I've always liked this kind of music.

52
00:03:30,484 --> 00:03:32,700
What do we do? What if we get caught?

53
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:35,116
Don't worry. Trust me.

54
00:03:41,388 --> 00:03:44,044
Is your real name Lim Jae Hong?

55
00:03:44,044 --> 00:03:46,788
It's a little old-fashioned, right?
So at home, she always goes,

56
00:03:46,788 --> 00:03:49,988
"Hong, Hong, Hong!"
That's what she always calls me.

57
00:03:49,988 --> 00:03:51,388
It sounds like a nickname.

58
00:03:51,388 --> 00:03:53,396
It is a nickname.

59
00:03:53,396 --> 00:03:56,564
Now I see why you two
have such a great relationship.

60
00:03:56,564 --> 00:03:58,332
People joke that...

61
00:03:58,332 --> 00:04:00,772
What, should I go get a bottle opener?

62
00:04:00,772 --> 00:04:03,183
No need. It's almost open.

63
00:04:03,183 --> 00:04:05,649
Come on, put some force into it.
Use some strength.

64
00:04:05,649 --> 00:04:07,028
I can do it.

65
00:04:07,028 --> 00:04:09,132
No, you can't.

66
00:04:09,132 --> 00:04:10,849
Yes, I can.

67
00:04:14,028 --> 00:04:15,849
- See? I told you it'd work!
- Awesome.

68
00:04:15,849 --> 00:04:17,816
Oh, seriously...

69
00:04:19,068 --> 00:04:21,460
Do you want to see this?

70
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:23,068
What is it?

71
00:04:23,068 --> 00:04:26,049
Just look at the front.
The back isn't finished yet.

72
00:04:27,084 --> 00:04:29,516
You drew this?

73
00:04:29,516 --> 00:04:33,476
Wow! Hey, I thought it was a photo.

74
00:04:33,476 --> 00:04:36,476
Wow, I had no idea you were this good.

75
00:04:36,476 --> 00:04:39,596
You're a total art genius!

76
00:04:39,596 --> 00:04:41,316
Wow!

77
00:04:41,316 --> 00:04:43,049
Did you design this too?

78
00:04:44,412 --> 00:04:46,500
I told you not to look at the back...

79
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:50,220
No way, it's way better than
my dad's ugly brown car!

80
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:55,180
Wow, you should start
your own car company someday.

81
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:58,116
My mom hates that I draw.

82
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:01,716
Dad says I can do whatever I want.

83
00:05:02,549 --> 00:05:05,308
But if Mom had supported me,

84
00:05:05,308 --> 00:05:07,649
Dad probably would've opposed it.

85
00:05:08,283 --> 00:05:12,076
Neither of them actually cares what I want.

86
00:05:12,076 --> 00:05:14,316
They just use me to fight with each other.

87
00:05:16,340 --> 00:05:20,249
So honestly, I was glad when they said
they were getting divorced.

88
00:05:20,249 --> 00:05:22,483
Because they seriously
fought every single day.

89
00:05:22,483 --> 00:05:25,172
Always yelling and cursing.

90
00:05:25,172 --> 00:05:27,596
Well, whenever that happened,

91
00:05:27,596 --> 00:05:30,249
I'd hide in the car and blast the music.

92
00:05:31,049 --> 00:05:32,883
And it made me feel a little better.

93
00:05:34,212 --> 00:05:36,916
You're lucky. Your parents get along.

94
00:05:41,783 --> 00:05:45,983
I'll take you for a drive someday.

95
00:05:47,788 --> 00:05:49,249
What? Why?

96
00:05:49,249 --> 00:05:53,849
We'll blast all that loud music you like.

97
00:05:55,084 --> 00:05:59,216
And just drive at,
like, 200 kilometers an hour.

98
00:06:00,868 --> 00:06:04,652
Why are you laughing? I'm serious.

99
00:06:04,652 --> 00:06:07,396
My dad teaches me how to drive sometimes.

100
00:06:07,396 --> 00:06:09,149
I'm actually pretty good.

101
00:06:59,716 --> 00:07:01,980
Now I think it was good to come.

102
00:07:01,980 --> 00:07:03,616
Right?

103
00:07:05,564 --> 00:07:07,149
Yeah.

104
00:07:11,583 --> 00:07:16,683
[Yejiii_star, Just the two of us #friend]

105
00:07:31,883 --> 00:07:34,883
[Min Seo]

106
00:07:38,849 --> 00:07:40,049
[Save]

107
00:07:40,049 --> 00:07:45,249
[Couple ring]

108
00:07:56,488 --> 00:07:58,172
What's going on?

109
00:07:58,172 --> 00:07:59,916
What is it? I don't know.

110
00:08:07,316 --> 00:08:10,849
[Calling...]

111
00:08:16,038 --> 00:08:18,849
Min Seo, are you okay?

112
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:21,236
I'm okay.

113
00:08:21,236 --> 00:08:22,852
Min Seo,

114
00:08:22,852 --> 00:08:26,249
can you come out and talk to Mom?

115
00:08:28,412 --> 00:08:30,692
Shall we go for a drive?

116
00:08:30,692 --> 00:08:32,348
A drive?

117
00:08:32,348 --> 00:08:34,629
Just like we talked about,

118
00:08:34,629 --> 00:08:37,149
blast the music

119
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:40,383
and drive really fast.

120
00:09:02,716 --> 00:09:06,316
My parents are both coming home late tonight.

121
00:09:09,561 --> 00:09:11,828
Lim Ye Ji! You're chickening out, right?

122
00:09:11,828 --> 00:09:13,747
No, I'm not!

123
00:09:13,747 --> 00:09:15,276
I told you.

124
00:09:15,276 --> 00:09:17,572
My dad taught me, so I'm really good.

125
00:09:17,572 --> 00:09:18,644
What are you saying?

126
00:09:18,644 --> 00:09:20,948
Seriously, can you do this?

127
00:09:20,948 --> 00:09:22,816
Of course!

128
00:09:24,922 --> 00:09:27,027
But where are we going?

129
00:09:33,924 --> 00:09:36,116
Is there somewhere you want to go?

130
00:09:37,268 --> 00:09:42,583
Maybe... somewhere with no people around?

131
00:09:46,816 --> 00:09:48,283
Hang on.

132
00:09:49,092 --> 00:09:51,828
Search for a quiet place with no people.

133
00:09:51,828 --> 00:09:54,092
Will that work?

134
00:09:54,092 --> 00:09:55,116
<i>In recent destinations,</i>

135
00:09:55,116 --> 00:09:57,204
[21 Bonggak-dong]
<i>there is a quiet place with no people.</i>

136
00:09:57,204 --> 00:09:58,676
<i>Shall I guide you there?</i>

137
00:09:58,676 --> 00:09:59,916
- See? It worked!
- No way!

138
00:09:59,916 --> 00:10:01,649
It really worked?

139
00:10:03,332 --> 00:10:07,283
<i>Starting navigation to a quiet place
with no people.</i>

140
00:10:14,686 --> 00:10:20,216
[Episode 3, A Quiet Place with No People]

141
00:11:05,156 --> 00:11:07,283
Jeez, seriously...

142
00:11:08,548 --> 00:11:09,802
What happened?

143
00:11:09,802 --> 00:11:12,649
Oh, Ye Ji, what happened to my car?

144
00:11:12,649 --> 00:11:14,103
Did you hear anything?

145
00:11:14,103 --> 00:11:15,583
Dad...

146
00:11:19,884 --> 00:11:22,183
What do I do?

147
00:12:06,532 --> 00:12:09,179
It's so heavy.

148
00:12:09,179 --> 00:12:10,716
No, I have to do it.

149
00:12:10,716 --> 00:12:12,716
For our Ye Ji.

150
00:12:13,988 --> 00:12:15,916
I'm sorry.

151
00:12:37,812 --> 00:12:39,449
This is killing me.

152
00:12:42,692 --> 00:12:46,994
[GPS Tracks Live]

153
00:12:46,994 --> 00:12:49,183
So this is your kind of place?

154
00:12:57,812 --> 00:12:59,396
I'm sorry.

155
00:12:59,396 --> 00:13:01,220
This is nuts!

156
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:02,996
It wasn't on purpose.

157
00:13:02,996 --> 00:13:04,649
Oh, jeez...

158
00:13:16,722 --> 00:13:18,973
Honey!

159
00:13:18,973 --> 00:13:20,308
Honey!

160
00:13:20,308 --> 00:13:21,849
Honey!

161
00:13:22,516 --> 00:13:24,049
Honey, honey, honey!

162
00:13:24,049 --> 00:13:25,583
It's me, me, me!

163
00:13:25,583 --> 00:13:27,788
It's Hong! Hong! Me, Hong!

164
00:13:27,788 --> 00:13:29,108
- Lim Jae Hong, Lim Jae...
- Yeah.

165
00:13:29,108 --> 00:13:33,216
What are you doing here looking like that?

166
00:13:33,216 --> 00:13:34,816
Quiet!

167
00:13:37,564 --> 00:13:39,828
What?

168
00:13:39,828 --> 00:13:42,332
Didn't Ye Ji tell you?

169
00:13:42,332 --> 00:13:44,279
Ye Ji?

170
00:13:44,279 --> 00:13:46,383
What about Ye Ji?

171
00:13:46,383 --> 00:13:48,249
What was I supposed to know?

172
00:13:49,116 --> 00:13:50,716
Well, it's...

173
00:13:53,780 --> 00:13:55,849
Our Ye Ji...

174
00:13:56,649 --> 00:13:58,516
She hit someone with the car.

175
00:14:00,902 --> 00:14:03,316
That kid took my car without telling me

176
00:14:03,316 --> 00:14:06,816
and looks like she got into an accident.

177
00:14:15,283 --> 00:14:17,316
Darn it!

178
00:14:28,172 --> 00:14:29,683
Hold on.

179
00:14:41,652 --> 00:14:44,308
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Oh, yes, Attorney Jo.

180
00:14:44,308 --> 00:14:47,416
- I'm so sorry for calling at this hour.
- <i>Yeah, it's okay.</i>

181
00:14:47,416 --> 00:14:48,783
- The thing is...
<i>- Yes.</i>

182
00:14:48,783 --> 00:14:51,964
Well... I mean...

183
00:14:51,964 --> 00:14:55,324
- A classmate of Min Seo's...
<i>- Yes.</i>

184
00:14:55,324 --> 00:14:58,804
The daughter of that parent's acquaintance...

185
00:14:58,804 --> 00:15:00,236
No, a son...

186
00:15:00,236 --> 00:15:02,949
<i>Oh, I see. That's quite a close connection.</i>

187
00:15:02,949 --> 00:15:06,316
Oh, yes. Very, very close.

188
00:15:06,316 --> 00:15:10,716
Anyway, the son drove the car out,

189
00:15:10,716 --> 00:15:12,988
and it seems he hit someone.

190
00:15:12,988 --> 00:15:15,932
But he was so shaken that he came home first.

191
00:15:15,932 --> 00:15:19,883
I wanted to know

192
00:15:19,883 --> 00:15:24,844
what would happen if he turned himself in.

193
00:15:24,844 --> 00:15:27,449
<i>Then what condition is the victim in?</i>

194
00:15:27,449 --> 00:15:29,020
<i>Injured or deceased?</i>

195
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:32,572
<i>If it's an injury, the severity
can greatly affect the sentence.</i>

196
00:15:32,572 --> 00:15:34,996
<i>So first, take measures to aid the victim.</i>

197
00:15:34,996 --> 00:15:36,483
Yes, understood, sir.

198
00:15:36,483 --> 00:15:40,020
Then... I'll assess the situation

199
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:41,180
and call you back...

200
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:43,283
<i>Director, just in case...</i>

201
00:15:43,283 --> 00:15:45,948
<i>- I'm saying this just in case.</i>
- Yeah.

202
00:15:45,948 --> 00:15:47,820
<i>This is purely hypothetical,</i>

203
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:50,996
<i>but if Min Seo's friend's
parent's acquaintance</i>

204
00:15:50,996 --> 00:15:54,052
<i>happens to be
in a custody dispute like you are...</i>

205
00:15:54,052 --> 00:15:56,188
C-Custody?

206
00:15:56,188 --> 00:15:59,868
<i>Yes, if they want to keep custody,
they need legal advice immediately.</i>

207
00:15:59,868 --> 00:16:03,436
<i>Otherwise, the court may see them
as an unfit parent.</i>

208
00:16:03,436 --> 00:16:07,149
<i>Then that could seriously hurt
their custody case.</i>

209
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:16,220
[Ye Ji]

210
00:16:17,932 --> 00:16:19,586
Just listen to what she says.

211
00:16:19,586 --> 00:16:21,516
She might be recording you.

212
00:16:25,643 --> 00:16:27,449
Oh, Ye Ji.

213
00:16:29,228 --> 00:16:31,404
<i>Min Seo,</i>

214
00:16:31,404 --> 00:16:34,316
<i>I'm sorry, it's my fault...</i>

215
00:16:35,222 --> 00:16:36,883
<i>Because of me...</i>

216
00:16:42,628 --> 00:16:43,812
Oh, his arm must hurt.

217
00:16:43,812 --> 00:16:46,420
No, tell me it's not true.

218
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:48,849
It can't be. No, no...

219
00:16:48,849 --> 00:16:50,916
- What do we do?
- Oh, dear, I'm sorry.

220
00:16:50,916 --> 00:16:53,716
Honey, let's take him to the hospital anyway.

221
00:16:53,716 --> 00:16:56,908
- Maybe he's still...
- It's no use.

222
00:16:56,908 --> 00:16:58,983
I already checked.

223
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:05,508
Our Ye Ji couldn't have done this!

224
00:17:05,508 --> 00:17:08,449
What do we do? What do we do?

225
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:11,616
Darn it...

226
00:17:14,932 --> 00:17:17,616
Don't tell me you're...

227
00:17:19,068 --> 00:17:22,283
Have you lost your mind?
What are you thinking?

228
00:17:23,108 --> 00:17:25,756
Then what am I supposed to do?

229
00:17:25,756 --> 00:17:27,683
Ye Ji suddenly came home
after causing an accident,

230
00:17:27,683 --> 00:17:30,268
crying and making a huge scene.

231
00:17:30,268 --> 00:17:33,716
I rushed over in shock too,
and I came here and saw that...

232
00:17:33,716 --> 00:17:37,004
that man was already dead.

233
00:17:37,004 --> 00:17:40,983
So am I supposed to report my own daughter?

234
00:17:43,732 --> 00:17:45,124
Why did you move him here?

235
00:17:45,124 --> 00:17:49,340
What if someone saw him lying out there?

236
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:52,324
Does moving him here make all this go away?

237
00:17:52,324 --> 00:17:53,508
Does it magically get hidden?

238
00:17:53,508 --> 00:17:55,612
I had to do something!

239
00:17:55,612 --> 00:17:57,283
I'm her father.

240
00:18:00,628 --> 00:18:02,216
Seriously...

241
00:18:20,276 --> 00:18:22,049
Let's have her turn herself in.

242
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:26,583
If we get a good lawyer
and have her turn herself in, then...

243
00:18:26,583 --> 00:18:29,483
You scared me!

244
00:18:32,083 --> 00:18:33,316
Turn herself in...

245
00:18:33,316 --> 00:18:35,849
Maybe it would be better
to have her turn herself in.

246
00:18:37,268 --> 00:18:40,716
Sorry, I have to take this.

247
00:18:43,756 --> 00:18:46,449
Yeah, Mr. Ha, what's the occasion...

248
00:18:48,444 --> 00:18:51,849
Chairwoman Jung, tomorrow?

249
00:18:54,108 --> 00:18:55,649
Oh, no. It's fine.

250
00:18:55,649 --> 00:18:57,668
[Missed Calls, Min Seo's Mother: 5]

251
00:18:57,668 --> 00:18:58,783
Rumors?

252
00:18:58,783 --> 00:19:00,108
[Min Seo's Mother (5), CEO Kim (5)]

253
00:19:00,108 --> 00:19:01,583
News article...

254
00:19:01,583 --> 00:19:03,852
Oh, I know, right?

255
00:19:03,852 --> 00:19:05,049
Well, that's something.

256
00:19:05,049 --> 00:19:07,416
[CEO Kim]

257
00:19:09,216 --> 00:19:10,732
[Why aren't you answering your phone?]
No, I understand completely.

258
00:19:10,732 --> 00:19:12,049
[People from Townhouse called]
Of course.

259
00:19:12,049 --> 00:19:13,509
[Writer Park wants to meet with you
for the Season 2 male lead]

260
00:19:13,509 --> 00:19:14,564
[Looks like Ryu Ji Su
and Kang Tae Han are out]

261
00:19:14,564 --> 00:19:16,416
Yeah, yeah. I know the place.

262
00:19:17,293 --> 00:19:19,483
